  "summary": "✅ Innovative design. Inspired technology. An industry-leading development studio. \nAchieving this means staying on the bleeding edge of technology, continually setting the standard for mobile applications, websites, backend development, 3D, VR, and design. \nFounded in 2008 by three pioneers in Internet and video game software development, Code Particle relentlessly pushes the boundaries of what’s possible — and remarkable — for you. \n\n✅ Our Customers:\nEstablished brands trust us with their full development projects, just as startups do trust us to rapidly enhance their internal team’s capabilities via our “onshore outsourcing.” \n\n✅ How we Manage Projects \nUnless you choose a Team Extension engagement, your project will be managed internally at Code Particle. \n\n✅ Technical Processes . \n1. Git, Branching & Pull Requests All our projects use git for source control. We prefer Atlassian Bitbucket but will adapt to whichever solution works best for the client. We have strict guidelines for commits, branching, tagging, versioning, and pull requests that we apply across all projects. A more detailed version of these guidelines can be made available if necessary. \n2. CI/CD, We build a CI/CD pipeline for each repository. Libraries get pushed to private artifact storage online. Actual components get dockerized and deployed automatically. \n3. Cloud Ops, We are experienced with AWS, Azure, GCP as well as custom hosting (such as Rackspace). We automate all of our deployments with technologies such as Terraform or Helm. \n\n✅ Architecture and Technical Design \nBefore implementation starts, each component is thoroughly designed and reviewed by peers. This includes: \n1. Architecture diagram \n2. Full description of business logic for the component \n3. Database Design with Data Models \n4. Swagger API file \n5. Class Diagram \n\n✅ API Documentation \n1. For each project if applicable, we set up a custom API documentation repository with a CI/CD pipeline that deploys a custom swagger site presenting all APIs. We typically break down our APIs in 3 categories: \n2. In design: manual swagger file, currently in design and not ready for development \n3. In development: manual swagger file, design is finalized and ready for development or currently in development \n4. Latest: swagger file automatically generated by the final implemented API \n5. Documentation Management \n6. This section details Code Particle’s guidelines for managing documentation. \n\n✅ Design \n1. Depending on your preference, we can provide designs in Figma, Sketch, Invision, and/or Zeplin but can use other tools.",
